              },
            ],
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Malin Keshar",
            text: _("Ick. Mudcrawlers. How did these things end up here?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Darken Volk",
            text: _("The magic of our world is unpredictable and random. Even without the interference of a trained mage, it sometimes coagulates by itself, giving rise to physical anomalies or breathing life into the inanimate. See there?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:clear_shroud",
            side: 1,
            xs: 25,
            ys: 4,
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:scroll_to",
            x: 25,
            y: 4,
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:delay",
            time: 1000,
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Darken Volk",
            text: _("It is merely a small eddy of energy, but enough to animate the swamp water."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Malin Keshar",
            text: _("I see. Well, even if these mudcrawlers are not much of a threat, they’re still bothersome. I wonder if I could be rid of them. What is magic mud even weak to, anyway? Fire?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Darken Volk",
            text: _("You should be able to figure it out on your own."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Malin Keshar",
            text: _("... I suppose you’re right."),
          },
        ],
      },
